From 6b1c94a3934ac51f6becdd7bbd46dde8db6db4a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JeyKul <77121325+JeyKul@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:33:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 50/56] PCI: exynos2200: Wi-Fi channel host driver

Channel 0 of the Exynos 2200's PCIe (gen2 x1, BCM4389 on the Galaxy S22
series): HSI1 power domain and TZPC restore, PHY (PMA/PCS) init, PERST#,
LTSSM through the ELBI glue, MSIs demultiplexed from the glue interrupt.
Sequences from Samsung's pcie-exynos-rc and S5E9925 cal code. No ASPM.
dw_handle_msi_irq() exported for the module.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
